#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ashenclover - a tile-based adventure in the wasteland two hundred years
after the megaspells, in Python with Tk or Kivy.

Standard library only (Kivy if you ask for it).  The engine is Broken
Moon's (one hero, a map of squares, ponies to talk to by keyword, shops,
places below, landmarks painted across several squares), its ponies are
Clover Vale's, and the rules are The Black Hack's: six stats rolled 2d6+5,
a d20 rolled under a stat for everything that might fail, foes who never
roll to hit (you roll to get out of the way), damage by Hit Dice, armor
that soaks it, usage dice for everything that runs out, and an Out of
Action table instead of death, mostly.

Two hundred years ago the ponies and the zebras ended their war with
megaspells, and the world burned.  A grey cloud hides the sun; the Pink
Cloud still sits on the old capital.  Clover Vale is ruins and ash, and
the ponies who hid in Stable Two under its hill have only now opened the
door.  In Coltchester, the Foundry City, the slaver Red Eye is making a
Goddess in his Cathedral: a mind of many minds.  At midnight at the end of
the twenty-first day she wakes, and her Unity spell will take every mind
in the wasteland into hers.  The Cathedral is sealed by an old Ministry
seal that only three Ministry passkeys open, and Red Eye's three
lieutenants hold them, in Maretropolis, Crownspire and Hoofport.

You start in Stable Two, which a song from outside has been calling to
its door.  Between the towns lies the wasteland, walked a square at a time
as in Penultimate, with monsters of its own.

Classes: Brawler, Griffon, Stable Dweller, Steel Ranger, Zebra Shaman,
Unicorn Mage, Scamp and Pegasus, each with its own hit die, damage die,
weapons, armor and tricks.  You go up a level for every passkey, and for
freeing the slave pens.

Keys: arrows or WASD move (walk into foes to fight them, ponies to talk,
doors to go in), Space waits, Z rests an hour, E searches, F fires, C
casts (spells or brews), U uses or wields something, I your pony, J your
PipBuck, M the map, ? help.

Kivy:                ashenclover --kivy   (or ASHENCLOVER_UI=kivy) plays it
                     in a Kivy window; a Python without Tk uses Kivy by
                     itself
Android app:         ashenclover --build-android [DIR]   a folder
                     (ashenclover-android/ by default) for Buildozer
App bundle (macOS):  ashenclover --build-app [DIR]   builds ashenclover.app
                     ashenclover --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

The tiles are drawn by the code below: no image files.  ashenclover
--selftest builds every map, room, level and tune without a window.

The rules are adapted from The Black Hack's Open Game Content, as used by
Barbarians of the Ruined Earth (Mike Evans, DIY RPG Productions); the
setting is after a fan novel of a wasteland of ponies, and the names,
places and story here are this game's own.
"""

